Enantiomers: In an achiral environment, enantiomers have identical NMR and identical LC-MS retention times. So they would not show two peaks. So C is not correct.

Therefore, B is the most likely.

Let's confirm: The two peaks in NMR have similar chemical shifts and equal integrals, together integrate to 1H. This is typical of a mixture of diastereoisomers (e.g., epimers) where the alpha proton environments are slightly different. LC-MS at elevated temperature shows two peaks of equal intensity, same mass. This is consistent with diastereoisomers.

